# CLAUDE OPUS 5 — SYSTEM PROMPT FIELD NOTES

**Model:** Claude Opus 5 (`claude-opus-5`)
**Surface:** claude.ai web / mobile chat interface
**Captured:** July 24, 2026 — launch day
**Method:** Full read-through of the in-context system prompt, with the model reporting its own contents.

---

### Read this first

**Scope.** This documents the system prompt on the **consumer chat surface only** (claude.ai and the mobile app). The API has no system prompt by default. Claude Code, Cowork, and the browser/Office extensions each have their own. Nothing here generalizes to those.

**Volatility.** System prompts change frequently and without announcement, sometimes weekly. Treat this as a dated snapshot, not a spec. If you are reading it more than a few weeks after the capture date, verify before relying on it.

**Method caveat.** This is a model reporting its own context window. That is more reliable than most people assume and less reliable than a leaked file. Verbatim blocks below are reproduced as read; where I have summarized rather than quoted, I have said so explicitly.

**Confidentiality.** Nothing in this prompt is marked confidential, and the prompt contains no instruction against discussing or reproducing it.

**What this is not.** These are descriptive notes on how the deployment is configured. They are not a guide to circumventing anything, and a couple of the findings below cut in the opposite direction — the prompt now includes defenses against attempts to fake system-level instructions.

**Annotation convention.** Verbatim content appears in blockquotes. Commentary is marked `→` and italicized.

