## A note on responsible use of this kind of document

Reading a system prompt is worth doing. It replaces folklore with fact, and a lot of community lore about these systems is wrong in ways that cause real frustration — people concluding a model "changed" when a session was routed, or that they were being condescended to by design when a reminder had been stapled onto their own message.

What it does not do is give you a lever to make the model act against its guidelines, and the prompt now contains an explicit defense against attempts to fake system-level instructions. Understanding why a model behaves a certain way is useful. Framing that understanding as a bypass is both less useful and less likely to work than it was six months ago.

